0..78 Comment "/// This source states the 2-sphere and the 3-sphere as presentations with one"
79..93 Comment "/// cell each."
94..97 Comment "///"
98..170 Comment "/// The 2-sphere has a point and a cell at the reflexivity of the point."
171..224 Comment "/// The 3-sphere has its cell one reflexivity higher."
225..304 Comment "/// The checker reads the path type at that wrapped point as the words over the"
305..343 Comment "/// cell, and the kernel replays them."
344..347 Comment "///"
348..427 Comment "/// The lowering mints the cancellation rules of a higher cell as it mints them"
428..443 Comment "/// for a loop."
444..494 Comment "/// No rule identifies a cell with the empty word."
495..498 Comment "///"
499..577 Comment "/// Limits: a case over a sphere needs a branch for its cell, and `Path.ap` on"
578..607 Comment "/// the cell needs that case."
608..611 Comment "///"
612..678 Comment "/// - see: #6395 — the case at a higher cell and `Path.ap` on it"
679..724 Comment "/// - see: corpus/model/identity/circle.gandr"
726..795 Comment "/// The 2-sphere has a point and a 2-cell at the point\'s reflexivity."
